   "page": "embedding",
   "title": "openprotein.embeddings",
   "sections": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "level": 0,
     "prose": "Create embeddings for your protein sequences using open-source and proprietary models! Note that for PoET Models, you will also need to supply a [`Prompt`](#openprotein.prompt.Prompt).",
     "entries": [],
     "autosummary": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "Interface",
     "level": 2,
     "prose": null,
     "entries": [
      {
       "directive": "autoclass",
       "target": "openprotein.embeddings.EmbeddingsAPI",
       "options": {
        "members": true
       }
      }
     ],
     "autosummary": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "Models",
     "level": 2,
     "prose": "These embedding models inherit from a base [`EmbeddingModel`](#openprotein.embeddings.EmbeddingModel), due to their shared functionality in providing the [`embed`](#openprotein.embeddings.EmbeddingModel.embed) method. These can also be used to fit the :ref:`transform-models`. .. _transform-models:",
     "entries": [
      {
       "directive": "autoclass",
       "target": "openprotein.embeddings.PoET2Model",
       "options": {
        "members": true,
        "inherited-members": true,
        "exclude-members": [
         "create",
         "get_model"
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "directive": "autoclass",
       "target": "openprotein.embeddings.PoETModel",
       "options": {
        "members": true,
        "inherited-members": true,
        "exclude-members": [
         "create",
         "get_model"
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "directive": "autoclass",
       "target": "openprotein.embeddings.AbLang2Model",
       "options": {
        "members": true,
        "inherited-members": true,
        "exclude-members": [
         "create",
         "get_model"
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "directive": "autoclass",
       "target": "openprotein.embeddings.OpenProteinModel",
       "options": {
        "members": true,
        "inherited-members": true,
        "exclude-members": [
         "create",
         "get_model"
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "directive": "autoclass",
       "target": "openprotein.embeddings.ESMModel",
       "options": {
        "members": true,
        "inherited-members": true,
        "exclude-members": [
         "create",
         "get_model"
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "directive": "autoclass",
       "target": "openprotein.embeddings.EmbeddingModel",
       "options": {
        "members": true
       }
      }
     ],
     "autosummary": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "Transform Models",
     "level": 3,
     "prose": "These models are overlaid on top of the base embeddings models to produce reduced/transformed embeddings. [`SVDModel`](#openprotein.svd.SVDModel) represents an SVD model which is suitable to reduce the high-dimensional embeddings returned by base embedding models, whilst maintaining semantic information, fitted on your [`AssayDataset`](#openprotein.data.AssayDataset). You can fit your own SVD from any model's [`fit_svd`](#openprotein.embeddings.EmbeddingModel.fit_svd). [`UMAPModel`](#openprotein.umap.UMAPModel) represents a UMAP model which is suitable to project the high-dimensional embeddings into a lower dimension (usually 2) for visualization, to understand the semantic grouping within your [`AssayDataset`](#openprotein.data.AssayDataset). You can fit your own UMAP from any model's [`fit_umap`](#openprotein.embeddings.EmbeddingModel.fit_umap).",
     "entries": [
      {
       "directive": "autoclass",
       "target": "openprotein.svd.SVDModel",
       "options": {
        "members": true,
        "inherited-members": true
       }
      },
      {
       "directive": "autoclass",
       "target": "openprotein.umap.UMAPModel",
       "options": {
        "members": true,
        "inherited-members": true
       }
      }
     ],
     "autosummary": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "Reduction methods",
     "level": 3,
     "prose": "Foundational embedding models also take an optional reduction to use simple pooling methods:",
     "entries": [
      {
       "directive": "autoclass",
       "target": "openprotein.common.ReductionType",
       "options": {
        "members": true
       }
      }
     ],
     "autosummary": []
    },
    {
